<title>USA: The top 10 movies at the U.S. weekend box office.</title>
<headline>The top 10 movies at the U.S. weekend box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-03-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the studios' estimated data for the top 10 movies at the March 7-9 box office, according to Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    1 (*) Private Parts .................... $15.1 million</p>
<p>    2 (*) Jungle 2 Jungle .................. $12.7 million</p>
<p>    3 (2) Donnie Brasco ....................  $8.2 million</p>
<p>    4 (1) The Empire Strikes Back ..........  $8.0 million</p>
<p>    5 (4) Booty Call .......................  $4.3 million</p>
<p>    6 (3) Star Wars ........................  $4.0 million</p>
<p>    7 (5) Absolute Power ...................  $3.7 million</p>
<p>    8 (6) Dante's Peak .....................  $3.3 million</p>
<p>    9 (7) Vegas Vacation ...................  $2.4 million</p>
<p>    10=(9) Marvin's Room ...................  $2.3 million</p>
<p>    10=(8) Fools Rush In ...................  $2.3 million</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Private Parts&quot; is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc..</p>
<p>Jungle 2 Jungle is released by Walt Disney Co.</p>
<p>&quot;Donnie Brasco,&quot; &quot;Booty Call,&quot; &quot;Absolute Power&quot; and &quot;Fools Rush In&quot; are released by Sony Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;The Empire Strikes Back&quot; and &quot;Star Wars&quot; are released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Dante's Peak&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd.</p>
<p>&quot;Vegas Vacation&quot; and &quot;Rosewood&quot; are released by Warner Bros., a unit of Time Warner Inc.</p>
<p>&quot;Marvin's Room&quot; is released by Disney's Miramax Films.</p>
</text>
